<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

<title>Course-to-Career Planner | Austin Coding Sample</title>

<style>

:root{
  --bg:#07110f;
  --panel:#0d1c19;
  --panel2:#122521;
  --panel3:#172e28;
  --cream:#f5efe1;
  --muted:#b9c8c1;
  --green:#72c49b;
  --green2:#3c9b70;
  --gold:#e6c77a;
  --blue:#74b9ff;
  --red:#e48b8b;
  --border:#28453d;
  --shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(0,0,0,.28);
  --radius:18px;
}

*{
  box-sizing:border-box;
  margin:0;
  padding:0;
}

html{
  scroll-behavior:smooth;
}

body{
  background:
    radial-gradient(circle at 10% 0%,rgba(114,196,155,.12),transparent 30%),
    radial-gradient(circle at 90% 20%,rgba(230,199,122,.08),transparent 25%),
    var(--bg);
  color:var(--cream);
  font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
  line-height:1.6;
}

button,
input,
select{
  font:inherit;
}

a{
  color:inherit;
}

.container{
  width:min(1200px,94%);
  margin:auto;
}

.hero{
  padding:70px 0 45px;
}

.hero-grid{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:1.4fr .8fr;
  gap:25px;
  align-items:stretch;
}

.hero-main,
.hero-side{
  background:linear-gradient(145deg,var(--panel2),var(--panel));
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:var(--radius);
  padding:34px;
  box-shadow:var(--shadow);
}

.eyebrow{
  color:var(--green);
  font-size:.78rem;
  font-weight:800;
  letter-spacing:.15em;
  text-transform:uppercase;
  margin-bottom:14px;
}

h1{
  font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4.4rem);
  line-height:1.02;
  margin-bottom:20px;
  max-width:800px;
}

.hero-main p{
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:1.08rem;
  max-width:760px;
}

.hero-side h3{
  margin-bottom:15px;
}

.hero-side ul{
  list-style:none;
}

.hero-side li{
  padding:10px 0;
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  color:var(--muted);
}

.hero-side li:last-child{
  border-bottom:0;
}

.check{
  color:var(--green);
  font-weight:900;
  margin-right:7px;
}

.section{
  padding:30px 0;
}

.section-heading{
  margin-bottom:25px;
}

.section-heading h2{
  font-size:2rem;
  margin-bottom:8px;
}

.section-heading p{
  color:var(--muted);
  max-width:800px;
}

.notice{
  background:rgba(230,199,122,.08);
  border:1px solid rgba(230,199,122,.3);
  border-left:5px solid var(--gold);
  padding:18px;
  border-radius:12px;
  color:#eadfca;
  margin-bottom:25px;
}

.control-bar{
  display:flex;
  flex-wrap:wrap;
  gap:10px;
  margin-bottom:25px;
}

.filter-btn{
  background:var(--panel2);
  color:var(--muted);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:10px 15px;
  border-radius:999px;
  cursor:pointer;
}

.filter-btn.active,
.filter-btn:hover{
  background:var(--green);
  color:#07110f;
  border-color:var(--green);
}

.course-grid{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);
  gap:20px;
}

.course-card{
  background:var(--panel);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:var(--radius);
  padding:24px;
  transition:.2s ease;
}

.course-card:hover{
  transform:translateY(-3px);
  border-color:var(--green2);
}

.course-card.selected{
  border:2px solid var(--green);
  box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(114,196,155,.08);
}

.course-top{
  display:flex;
  justify-content:space-between;
  gap:15px;
  margin-bottom:15px;
}

.course-title{
  font-size:1.35rem;
  font-weight:800;
}

.tag{
  display:inline-block;
  padding:5px 9px;
  border-radius:999px;
  font-size:.72rem;
  font-weight:800;
  margin:3px;
}

.free{
  background:rgba(114,196,155,.13);
  color:var(--green);
}

.paid{
  background:rgba(230,199,122,.12);
  color:var(--gold);
}

.austin{
  background:rgba(116,185,255,.12);
  color:var(--blue);
}

.course-card p{
  color:var(--muted);
  margin-bottom:15px;
}

.metrics{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
  gap:8px;
  margin:18px 0;
}

.metric{
  background:var(--panel3);
  padding:12px;
  border-radius:10px;
}

.metric small{
  display:block;
  color:#91a59d;
  font-size:.7rem;
  text-transform:uppercase;
}

.metric strong{
  display:block;
  margin-top:3px;
}

.course-card h4{
  color:var(--green);
  margin:18px 0 7px;
}

.course-card ul{
  padding-left:20px;
  color:var(--muted);
}

.course-card li{
  margin-bottom:5px;
}

.button-row{
  display:flex;
  flex-wrap:wrap;
  gap:9px;
  margin-top:20px;
}

.btn{
  display:inline-block;
  border:0;
  border-radius:9px;
  padding:11px 15px;
  cursor:pointer;
  text-decoration:none;
  font-weight:800;
}

.btn-primary{
  background:var(--green);
  color:#07110f;
}

.btn-secondary{
  background:transparent;
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  color:var(--cream);
}

.btn-secondary:hover{
  border-color:var(--green);
}

.dashboard{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
  gap:20px;
}

.panel{
  background:var(--panel);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:var(--radius);
  padding:25px;
}

.panel h3{
  margin-bottom:8px;
}

.panel-sub{
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:.92rem;
  margin-bottom:20px;
}

.score{
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:20px;
}

.score-circle{
  width:105px;
  height:105px;
  border-radius:50%;
  border:8px solid var(--green2);
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;
  font-size:1.6rem;
  font-weight:900;
  flex-shrink:0;
}

.progress-wrap{
  flex:1;
}

.progress{
  height:12px;
  background:#20342f;
  border-radius:999px;
  overflow:hidden;
}

.progress-bar{
  height:100%;
  width:0%;
  background:var(--green);
  transition:.3s;
}

.checklist{
  list-style:none;
}

.checklist li{
  display:flex;
  gap:10px;
  align-items:flex-start;
  padding:11px 0;
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
}

.checklist li:last-child{
  border-bottom:0;
}

.checklist input{
  margin-top:5px;
  accent-color:var(--green);
}

.schedule{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:repeat(7,1fr);
  gap:8px;
  margin-top:20px;
}

.day{
  background:var(--panel3);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:12px;
  padding:12px;
  min-height:150px;
}

.day strong{
  display:block;
  color:var(--green);
  margin-bottom:8px;
}

.day p{
  font-size:.82rem;
  color:var(--muted);
  margin-bottom:7px;
}

.hours-form{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
  gap:12px;
  margin-top:20px;
}

.field label{
  display:block;
  font-size:.78rem;
  color:var(--muted);
  margin-bottom:5px;
}

.field input,
.field select{
  width:100%;
  background:#081512;
  color:var(--cream);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:8px;
  padding:10px;
}

.total-box{
  background:var(--panel3);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:18px;
  border-radius:12px;
  margin-top:15px;
}

.total-box strong{
  color:var(--green);
  font-size:1.4rem;
}

.pathway{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);
  gap:12px;
}

.step{
  position:relative;
  background:var(--panel3);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:20px;
  border-radius:14px;
}

.step-number{
  width:35px;
  height:35px;
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;
  background:var(--green);
  color:#07110f;
  border-radius:50%;
  font-weight:900;
  margin-bottom:12px;
}

.step h3{
  margin-bottom:7px;
}

.step p{
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:.9rem;
}

.project-grid{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
  gap:15px;
}

.project{
  background:var(--panel);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:15px;
  padding:20px;
}

.project .level{
  color:var(--gold);
  font-size:.75rem;
  font-weight:800;
  text-transform:uppercase;
}

.project h3{
  margin:8px 0;
}

.project p{
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:.9rem;
}

.project ul{
  margin:12px 0 0 18px;
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:.87rem;
}

.job-table-wrap{
  overflow-x:auto;
}

table{
  width:100%;
  border-collapse:collapse;
  min-width:850px;
}

th,
td{
  padding:14px;
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  text-align:left;
  vertical-align:top;
}

th{
  color:var(--green);
  background:var(--panel3);
}

td{
  color:var(--muted);
}

details{
  background:var(--panel);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:12px;
  margin-bottom:10px;
}

summary{
  cursor:pointer;
  padding:16px;
  font-weight:800;
}

.details-content{
  padding:0 18px 18px;
  color:var(--muted);
}

.tracker{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);
  gap:12px;
}

.tracker-item{
  background:var(--panel3);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:15px;
  border-radius:12px;
}

.tracker-item label{
  display:flex;
  gap:9px;
  align-items:center;
  color:var(--muted);
}

.tracker-item input{
  accent-color:var(--green);
}

.application-table input,
.application-table select{
  width:100%;
  min-width:120px;
  background:#07110f;
  color:var(--cream);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:8px;
  border-radius:7px;
}

.footer{
  padding:50px 0 80px;
  color:#91a59d;
  font-size:.85rem;
}

.hidden{
  display:none!important;
}

@media(max-width:900px){

  .hero-grid,
  .dashboard,
  .course-grid{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
  }

  .pathway{
    grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);
  }

  .project-grid{
    grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
  }

  .schedule{
    grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);
  }
}

@media(max-width:600px){

  .hero{
    padding-top:35px;
  }

  .hero-main,
  .hero-side,
  .panel,
  .course-card{
    padding:20px;
  }

  .metrics,
  .hours-form,
  .project-grid,
  .tracker{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
  }

  .pathway{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
  }

  .schedule{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
  }

  h1{
    font-size:2.3rem;
  }
}

</style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

<!-- =========================================================
     HERO
========================================================= -->

<section class="hero">

  <div class="hero-grid">

    <div class="hero-main">

      <div class="eyebrow">
        Pathkeeper • Course-to-Career Template
      </div>

      <h1>
        Don't just choose a course.
        Build a path from learning to employment.
      </h1>

      <p>
        This sample shows how a person can evaluate an inexpensive or free
        coding program, understand exactly what it covers, turn the learning
        into portfolio evidence, create a realistic study schedule, and
        compare the resulting skills against actual Austin-area job requirements.
      </p>

      <div class="button-row">

        <button
          class="btn btn-primary"
          onclick="scrollToSection('course-selection')">
          Compare Courses
        </button>

        <button
          class="btn btn-secondary"
          onclick="scrollToSection('planner')">
          Build My Schedule
        </button>

      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="hero-side">

      <h3>The decision system</h3>

      <ul>

        <li>
          <span class="check">01</span>
          Define the employment target
        </li>

        <li>
          <span class="check">02</span>
          Compare course coverage
        </li>

        <li>
          <span class="check">03</span>
          Calculate time and cost
        </li>

        <li>
          <span class="check">04</span>
          Build projects while learning
        </li>

        <li>
          <span class="check">05</span>
          Create portfolio evidence
        </li>

        <li>
          <span class="check">06</span>
          Start applying before you feel "finished"
        </li>

      </ul>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     HOW TO USE
========================================================= -->

<section class="section">

  <div class="notice">

    <strong>Important:</strong>
    A course is not the same thing as a job qualification.
    This planner deliberately separates course completion from
    job readiness. The goal is to identify what the course teaches,
    what must be learned elsewhere, what evidence must be built,
    and what employers are actually requesting.

  </div>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     COURSE SELECTION
========================================================= -->

<section class="section" id="course-selection">

  <div class="section-heading">

    <h2>1. Compare learning options</h2>

    <p>
      The sample below focuses on web development and adjacent technology
      because Austin has demand for web, front-end, WordPress, software and
      IT-related roles. It intentionally includes completely free resources,
      structured free resources, and paid options.
    </p>

  </div>

  <div class="control-bar">

    <button
      class="filter-btn active"
      onclick="filterCourses('all',this)">
      All
    </button>

    <button
      class="filter-btn"
      onclick="filterCourses('free',this)">
      Free
    </button>

    <button
      class="filter-btn"
      onclick="filterCourses('low',this)">
      Low Cost
    </button>

    <button
      class="filter-btn"
      onclick="filterCourses('austin',this)">
      Austin
    </button>

    <button
      class="filter-btn"
      onclick="filterCourses('javascript',this)">
      JavaScript
    </button>

  </div>


  <div class="course-grid">


    <!-- MDN -->

    <article class="course-card"
      data-type="free javascript"
      data-course="MDN Web Development">

      <div class="course-top">

        <div class="course-title">
          MDN Learn Web Development
        </div>

        <div>
          <span class="tag free">FREE</span>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Mozilla's structured web-development curriculum.
        Particularly useful for understanding the fundamentals rather than
        simply copying projects.
      </p>

      <div class="metrics">

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Cost</small>
          <strong>$0</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Schedule</small>
          <strong>Self-paced</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Level</small>
          <strong>Beginner</strong>
        </div>

      </div>

      <h4>Coverage</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>Environment setup</li>
        <li>Web standards</li>
        <li>Semantic HTML</li>
        <li>CSS fundamentals</li>
        <li>CSS layout and responsive design</li>
        <li>JavaScript fundamentals</li>
        <li>Accessibility</li>
        <li>Version control concepts</li>
        <li>Testing and performance concepts</li>
        <li>Publishing websites</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Portfolio opportunities</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>Responsive business website</li>
        <li>Accessible information site</li>
        <li>Interactive JavaScript tool</li>
        <li>Data-driven resource page</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>What it does NOT automatically provide</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>Job placement</li>
        <li>Local employer network</li>
        <li>Large capstone portfolio</li>
        <li>Professional work experience</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="button-row">

        <a
          class="btn btn-primary"
          href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development"
          target="_blank">
          Open MDN
        </a>

        <button
          class="btn btn-secondary"
          onclick="selectCourse('MDN Web Development')">
          Select
        </button>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- Odin -->

    <article class="course-card"
      data-type="free javascript"
      data-course="The Odin Project">

      <div class="course-top">

        <div class="course-title">
          The Odin Project
        </div>

        <div>
          <span class="tag free">FREE</span>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Project-heavy curriculum designed around building websites and
        applications instead of only consuming lessons.
      </p>

      <div class="metrics">

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Cost</small>
          <strong>$0</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Schedule</small>
          <strong>Self-paced</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Path</small>
          <strong>Full Stack JS</strong>
        </div>

      </div>

      <h4>Coverage</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>HTML</li>
        <li>CSS</li>
        <li>JavaScript</li>
        <li>DOM manipulation</li>
        <li>APIs</li>
        <li>Git and GitHub</li>
        <li>Node.js</li>
        <li>Back-end concepts</li>
        <li>Testing</li>
        <li>Multiple portfolio projects</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Portfolio opportunities</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>Landing page recreation</li>
        <li>JavaScript application</li>
        <li>API-powered application</li>
        <li>Full-stack application</li>
        <li>Responsive multi-page site</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Best use</h4>

      <p>
        Strong choice when the learner wants a substantial portfolio and
        eventually wants to move beyond basic static websites.
      </p>

      <div class="button-row">

        <a
          class="btn btn-primary"
          href="https://www.theodinproject.com/paths"
          target="_blank">
          Open Odin
        </a>

        <button
          class="btn btn-secondary"
          onclick="selectCourse('The Odin Project')">
          Select
        </button>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- freeCodeCamp -->

    <article class="course-card"
      data-type="free javascript"
      data-course="freeCodeCamp">

      <div class="course-top">

        <div class="course-title">
          freeCodeCamp
        </div>

        <div>
          <span class="tag free">FREE</span>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Large interactive curriculum with coding exercises, certifications,
        projects and multiple development paths.
      </p>

      <div class="metrics">

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Cost</small>
          <strong>$0</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Schedule</small>
          <strong>Flexible</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Format</small>
          <strong>Interactive</strong>
        </div>

      </div>

      <h4>Coverage to investigate</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>Responsive web design</li>
        <li>JavaScript</li>
        <li>Front-end libraries</li>
        <li>Data structures</li>
        <li>Back-end development</li>
        <li>APIs</li>
        <li>Databases</li>
        <li>Multiple project-based certifications</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Portfolio opportunities</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>Portfolio website</li>
        <li>Interactive tools</li>
        <li>JavaScript applications</li>
        <li>API applications</li>
        <li>Front-end projects</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Important strategy</h4>

      <p>
        Do not treat certificate completion as the final product.
        Convert the lessons into original projects with your own
        requirements, interface decisions and documentation.
      </p>

      <div class="button-row">

        <a
          class="btn btn-primary"
          href="https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/"
          target="_blank">
          Open freeCodeCamp
        </a>

        <button
          class="btn btn-secondary"
          onclick="selectCourse('freeCodeCamp')">
          Select
        </button>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- Google -->

    <article class="course-card"
      data-type="low"
      data-course="Google IT Automation with Python">

      <div class="course-top">

        <div class="course-title">
          Google IT Automation with Python
        </div>

        <div>
          <span class="tag paid">PAID / FINANCIAL AID OPTIONS</span>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        A different route from front-end development: Python, Git,
        automation and IT-oriented programming.
      </p>

      <div class="metrics">

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Typical U.S. Price</small>
          <strong>$49/mo</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Estimated</small>
          <strong>~6 months</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="metric">
          <small>Study</small>
          <strong>~10 hrs/wk</strong>
        </div>

      </div>

      <h4>Coverage</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>Python</li>
        <li>Git and GitHub</li>
        <li>Automation</li>
        <li>Operating systems</li>
        <li>Regular expressions</li>
        <li>Configuration management</li>
        <li>Cloud concepts</li>
        <li>IT automation</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Portfolio opportunities</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>File automation tool</li>
        <li>Data-cleaning script</li>
        <li>System monitoring utility</li>
        <li>API automation project</li>
        <li>Deployment/configuration project</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Best use</h4>

      <p>
        Better fit for someone interested in Python, IT automation and
        technical operations than someone whose immediate target is
        front-end web development.
